<h3>Prototype editor</h3>

<p>
    The <strong>prototype editor</strong> is the tool to create and edit prototypes of checklists.
</p>
<p>
    The <strong>visual editor</strong> shows the elements of the checklist: the header, the pages, the groups, the sub-groups and the items.
</p>
<p>
    Each element can be selected with a click. A click on the title selects the whole prototype. If an element is selected, a tool bar for that element is show.
</p>
<p>
    The <strong>property panel</strong> shows a list of properties of the selected element. The properties describe the element behavior. their values can be set for prototype with state <strong>draft</strong> using, following the instructions given therein.
</p>

<h4>Editor commands</h4>

<table>
    <tr><td>ADD GROUP</td><td>Adds a new group to the current page.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-plus"></i></td><td>Adds a new page to the prototype or a new item to a selected group.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-cog"></i></td><td>Shows the <strong>property panel</strong>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-trash-o"></i></td><td>Delete the selected element.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-arrow-down"></i></td><td>Moves the selected element down or the selected page to the right.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-arrow-up"></i></td><td>Moves the selected element up or the selected page to the left.</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Actions</h4>

<table>
    <tr><td>Save</td><td>Saves the changes of the prototype.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Obsolete</td><td>Shows the steps of the obsolescence workflow.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Submit for obsol.</td><td>Creates a obsolescence workflow to change the state from <strong>active</strong> or <strong>approved</strong> to <strong>obsolete</strong>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Approve</td><td>Shows the steps of the approval workflow.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Submit for approval</td><td>Changes the state of the prototype from <strong>in simulation</strong> to <strong>in approval</strong> and creates the approval workflow.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Delete</td><td>Deletes a <strong>draft</strong> prototype.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cancel simulation</td><td>Changes the state of the prototype from <strong>in simulation</strong> back to <strong>draft</strong>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Start simulation</td><td>Changes the state of the prototype from <strong>draft</strong> to <strong>in simulation</strong>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Preview</td><td>Creates a test instance, if the prototype has state <strong>draft</strong>, or a simulation evidence instance, if the prototype has state <strong>in simulation</strong>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>History</td><td>Shows the history of the prototype.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Quit</td><td>Closes the prototype editor and returns to the page prototypes list.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-database-o"></i></td><td>Shows the data sources of the prototype.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><i class="fi flaticon-calculator"></i></td><td>Shows the expression editor.</td></tr>
</table>